parameters.text:
=Here is the data given by the clients about themselves in the type form, which is then saved to Google Sheets, which I brought out to you. After seeing this data mention if they are to be put in the cold leads or hot leads category. 

---

timestamp : {{ $json.Timestamp }}
fullName : {{ $json['Full Name'] }}
workEmail : {{ $json['Work Email'] }}
companyName : {{ $json['Company Name'] }}
companySize : {{ $json['Company Size (Employees)'] }}
industry : {{ $json.Industry }}
whatTheyLookingToMonitor : {{ $json['What are you looking to monitor?'] }}
jobTitleORrole : {{ $json['Job Title / Role'] }}

---

I can also tell you what a good fit is.
->Company size: 50-2000 employees (too small = no budget, too big = they have their own tooling already and a 6-month procurement cycle)
->Industry: tech/SaaS, fintech, or e-commerce — we don't have great luck outside those
->They used a work email, not a Gmail/Yahoo address (we get a lot of students and tire-kickers using personal emails)
->Bonus points if the "company size" or "what are you looking to monitor" field in the form shows they have real infra (mentions Kubernetes, AWS, multiple services, etc.) vs. someone just curious
For the leads that don't qualify, don't just delete them — drop them into a list we can run a monthly nurture email to. Maybe someday they'll be big enough.
All we currently have is: form submissions landing in a Google Sheet (Typeform → Sheet), and a Slack channel called #hot-leads where reps currently get pinged manually. 
So make it short and give the reason why it is hot/cold lead.

=Full Name -> {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json["Full Name"] }}
Work Email -> {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json["Work Email"] }}
Company Name/Industry/Size -> {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json["Company Name"] }} in {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json.Industry }} ( {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json['Company Size (Employees)'] }} employees )
What does they want to be monitored -> {{ $('Triggered When Someone fills the typeform and a row appended').item.json['What are you looking to monitor?'] }}
Reason for becoming a hot lead : {{ $json.output.reason }}
